Acceptance criteria:
The actual default straight play pose exposes blue/cyan shell corners under
the table lamp alone at desktop and phone sizes. Samples must hit physical
shell surfaces, not background or LCDs. Switching all lights off remains dark;
room lighting still works. LCDs remain unlit, non-tone-mapped surfaces.
Keep existing camera fit, collision clearance, Inspect/locked angles, stylus,
native input and loading behavior. Preserve the existing parked coverage debt,
unrelated dirty images and frozen published book. Publication needs exact-SHA
deployment and actual public-site verification, separate from local evidence.

Completion evidence:
Investigation: old straight play at (5,5.1,8) places the front-facing shell
ahead of the lamp's emitting region. Table-lamp-only samples are blue9 on
the lid and10 on the deck. Enlarging tabletop bounce alone is ineffective.
Initial lit target (-2,5.1,-2) exposes a full-rotation collision risk:
the existing Inspect placement regression reports rotation gap -1.047.
One bounded correction moves the shared target to (-2,5.1,-8).
Final lamp-only lid blue108-113/deck117-157; all eight rays hit real shell.
All eight go RGB0,0,0 with every lamp off. No material/light/exposure edits.
Rendered960x720final default pose inspected; not owner aesthetic approval.
Syntax, all61unit tests and static build pass. Final six-case browser run
passes1.6m: real native dual-screen input/stylus, locked gameplay/hinge,
phone fit, pickup/full-rotation clearance/live Inspect/branding, and both
new default-upright desktop/phone lighting cases. Immediate upload/native
handoff also passed before the final clearance-only position correction.
The new fixture's first attempt incorrectly treats powered-off reflective
LCD glass as unlit. Its one bounded repair uses the controller's real static
status LCDs; real native LCD/input behavior is qualified separately above.
No new skips, weaker assertions, timeout changes or reduced pixel ratio.
Technical completion is separate from pending authorized publication:
commit/push, exact-SHA Pages and public-site checks go in the final issue
receipt, not an endless receipt-only documentation/deployment loop.

